Exact source: skills/productivity/google-workspace/scripts/google_api.py
- drive_get: client.rs adapts the one-file-ID metadata GET and explicit field
  projection. Anima replaces parent/owner/provider-link fields with version,
  trashed and canDownload, validates the returned exact ID, and constructs a
  stable source link itself. No arbitrary provider URLs are followed.
- drive_download: client.rs adapts the metadata-first export/download branch.
  Google Documents use text/plain export; stored text/plain uses alt=media.
  Anima rewrites this useful endpoint/format behavior in Rust, reads capped
  bytes in memory, and does not copy the upstream default PDF/CSV/PNG map,
  local-path creation or unbounded MediaIoBaseDownload loop.
- drive_search: only the selected metadata result shape informs native search.
  Anima does not copy files.list, raw q or fullText-query interpolation. Search
  performs exact selected-ID metadata GETs and literal filename matching.

This is selected code/behavior adaptation, not full Google workspace parity.
Python clients, optional gws subprocesses, token JSON files, configuration and
profiles are neither read nor executed. tools/drive_preview_tool.py is desktop
browser control and is not credited as Google Drive integration.

Anima uses its independent generation-bound credential vault and owner-selected
1-16-ID authority. Provider drive.readonly consent is broader than that native
selection. No Drive writes, sharing, deletion, sync or whole-account enumeration
is provided. Existing Gmail and Calendar credentials remain separate.

